<title>POLAND: Polish minimum T-bill prices flat at tender.</title>
<headline>Polish minimum T-bill prices flat at tender.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Minimum prices of all Polish T-bills held flat at today's primary auction, after rising over recent weeks, on total demand of 907 million zlotys against a 800 million zloty offer, the finance ministry said.</p>
<p>The ministry sold bills worth 525 million zlotys.  </p>
<p>   T-bill	    8-week  13-week  26-week  39-week  52-week</p>
<p>   new min price    ---     95.28    90.90     ---     83.20</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.28)  (90.90)    ---    (83.20)</p>
<p>   new max price    ---     95.41    91.02     ---     83.32</p>
<p>   (pvs auction)    ---    (95.50)  (91.10)    ---    (83.35)</p>
<p>   offer		---     300.0    100.0     ---     400.0</p>
<p>   bids recorded    ---     490.1     60.9     ---     355.7</p>
<p>   bids accepted    ---     300.0     43.3     ---     181.9</p>
<p>   next auction     ---     300.0    100.0     ---     400.0</p>
<p>NOTE. Offer and all bids in million zlotys.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
